# ── Runtime data written by the print server (NEVER commit) ──────────────────
# DATA_DIR defaults to print-server/ itself for legacy script installs, so a
# live install writes all of the following INSIDE the working tree. Only
# clubbers*.csv used to be ignored, which meant a `git add -A` — or a fork
# owner sending a pull request from a machine that had run the server —
# published the church's Pusher app secret, the phone PIN, every child's
# check-in history and the full household export.
#
# The Electron app points AWANA_DATA_DIR at userData instead, so these paths
# only appear for script installs and local development. They are ignored
# regardless of which directory they turn up in.

# Roster and household exports (names, birthdates, allergies, guardians, phones)
clubbers*.csv
households*.csv
!print-server/clubbers-template.csv

# config.json holds pusherSecret and phonePin
config.json
!electron-app/renderer/*config*.json

# Check-in history, attendance and the event replay buffer (names + timestamps)
print-history.json
print-history.json.tmp
attendance.json
events-buffer.json

# Generated label images / temp print artifacts
label-*.png
label-*.html
awana-label-*.png
awana-worksheet-*.pdf

# Example/test files
example.html
example_files/

# Claude Code session data
.claude/
